The repository's first-party license does not relicense these materials.

## Source-specific terms and citations

See [SOURCES.md](SOURCES.md) for each bundled document's title, edition, original
publisher, authoritative source, citation key, rights evidence, and release
disposition. The corresponding bibliography is
[doc/framework-references.bib](../../doc/framework-references.bib).

Preserve the original copyright, attribution, license, and other required notices.
Where an applicable government-work exception exists, assess its scope and
jurisdiction and any separately protected third-party content. Do not apply one
blanket license or noncommercial-use rule to this mixed corpus.

Educational, research, or noncommercial intent does not itself grant permission
to copy, convert, upload to model services, include in a retrieval system, or
redistribute a publisher's material. Check terms for the intended activity.
Citation is required scholarly attribution, not a substitute for permission.
See [THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](../../THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) for the project-wide
licensing distinctions and publication gate.

## Conversion and accuracy

The repository records conversion from original documents to Markdown using
[Docling](https://github.com/docling-project/docling), for evaluation research.
Converted text may contain formatting changes, omissions, or errors. Conversion
does not transfer ownership, create reuse rights, or establish that meaning and
requirements have been preserved accurately.

Credit the source publisher and conversion tool separately. Verify important
claims against the authoritative original, retain the source edition/as-of date,
and distinguish proposals, historical versions, and guidance from current law.
No publisher endorsement or legal/compliance advice is implied.

## Publication status

The presence of a document in this repository is not proof that its redistribution
has been cleared. Review the source-specific register before releasing a source
snapshot, excerpts, retrieval contexts, or model outputs containing source text.
The raw-export ignore rules do not remove framework files already in the
repository or its history. Do not redistribute uncleared material merely because
this notice accompanies it.

